//@version=6
// =====================================================================================
// LIVE TREND DETECTOR
//
// A "live trend" = a directional run that, over a stretch of time (however long it takes),
// covers a meaningful distance AND is CLEAN (not zig-zag). Cleanliness = R-squared of an
// OLS fit: bars hugging the fit line = straight trend; scattered = chop, rejected.
// Steepness is IRRELEVANT -- a slow shallow grind that stays on its line is a trend just
// as much as a sharp plunge. Total run + straightness qualify it, not slope.
//
// STATE MACHINE (this is the key difference from a level-detector):
//   FLAT  -- scan windows winMin..winMax. When a clean run (R^2 >= minR2) reaches runMinPts
//            (>=150 default) we LATCH a live trend: lock the anchor bar, the slope, the
//            direction. Fire the start dot.
//   LIVE  -- 150pts is only the TRIGGER, not the end. Each bar we REFIT the OLS over the
//            whole live window (anchor->now) to keep the live slope/R^2 diagnostics current.
//            The trend stays alive until a big pullback (below); it tolerates pauses (incl.
//            overnight) so a multi-hour descent = one trend. (No line is drawn -- the start
//            and break dots plus the data-window columns carry the concept; a single OLS
//            line across a long, bent, dynamic-pullback trend cut across price and looked
//            wrong, so line drawing was removed.)
//   BREAK -- ends ONLY on a BIG pullback: price retraces effPullback off the extreme (a real
//            reversal), where effPullback = max(pullbackPts, travel * pullbackFrac) so a far-
//            travelled runner needs a proportionally bigger reversal to end. The live refit
//            does NOT decide the break, so a trend never ends at its own low/high on a fit
//            metric. Drop an end dot at the confirmation bar, arm a same-direction lock.
//   LOCK  -- after a break we BLOCK a new trend in the SAME direction until price retraces
//            reEntryFrac of the completed move back off its extreme (a real reversal). This
//            is what stops a long clean grind from being re-detected as N marches 100->240.
//
// Math: over the last N bars, x = 0 (oldest) .. N-1 (current), y = price.
//   slope = cov(x,y)/var(x)   R^2 = cov(x,y)^2/(var(x)*var(y))   run = |slope|*(N-1)
// Pure detector -- no trades. Eyeball first.
// =====================================================================================
indicator("Live Trend Detector", overlay=true, max_labels_count=500, max_bars_back=2000)

//=============================
// Inputs
//=============================
winMin     = input.int(60,  "Scan window MIN (bars)", minval=5,  maxval=1000, group="Trend window")
winMax     = input.int(240, "Scan window MAX (bars)", minval=5,  maxval=1000, group="Trend window")
winStep    = input.int(10,  "Scan step (bars)",       minval=1,  maxval=50,   group="Trend window")

runMinPts  = input.float(150.0, "Min run size to TRIGGER a trend (pts, fit-line net move)", minval=1.0, step=5.0, group="Trend qualification")
minR2      = input.float(0.75,  "Min R-squared (straightness; 1 = perfect line)", minval=0.1, maxval=1.0, step=0.05, group="Trend qualification")
srcPrice   = input.source(close, "Price source for the fit", group="Trend qualification")
pickBest   = input.bool(true, "Detect on BEST-fitting window (else first qualifying)", group="Trend qualification")

pullbackPts = input.float(150.0, "Break: retrace this many pts off the trend extreme (big pullback = real reversal)", minval=1.0, step=5.0, group="Trend break")
// DYNAMIC pullback: a trend that has already travelled far deserves more room before we call a
// reversal -- a static 150pt dip shouldn't end a 600pt run (that chops a continuing trend into
// fragments and then the re-entry lock blocks the continuation). Effective pullback each bar =
// max(pullbackPts, travel * pullbackFrac), where travel = |extreme - startPrice|. It ratchets
// UP only (travel only grows as the extreme extends). 0 = OFF (pure static pullbackPts).
pullbackFrac = input.float(0.5, "Break: dynamic pullback = max(base, travel x this). 0=off, ~0.5 lets runners run", minval=0.0, maxval=2.0, step=0.05, group="Trend break")
reEntryFrac = input.float(0.7,  "Re-entry block: after a break, block a SAME-direction trend until price retraces this fraction of the completed move", minval=0.0, maxval=1.0, step=0.05, group="Trend break")
liveCap     = input.int(1500,   "Safety cap on live window length (bars) — protects Pine calc time", minval=100, maxval=1990, group="Trend break")
// CONFIRMATION WINDOW: a latch on the tail of a dying move often reverses immediately (caught
// the bottom/top). Within confirmMins bars of the START dot, if price moves AGAINST the trend by
// >= confirmAdvPts (measured from the dot's close), CANCEL the latch -- it was a false start. A
// cancel does NOT arm the re-entry lock, so the direction can re-fire as soon as a fresh clean
// window qualifies. 0 mins = OFF. Try ~10-20 min / ~40 pt.
confirmMins   = input.int(0, "Confirm window (bars/min): cancel if it reverses within this (0=off)", minval=0, maxval=120, group="Trend break")
confirmAdvPts = input.float(40.0, "Confirm: cancel if adverse move >= this (pts) inside the window", minval=1.0, step=5.0, group="Trend break")
// UN-TIMED ADVERSE STOP (replaces the time-boxed confirm window). Cancel the latch if price
// moves >= adverseStopPts AGAINST the dot close at ANY age -- catches SLOW failures the fixed
// confirm window misses (a trend that only crosses 40pt adverse at bar 31+ slips past a 30-bar
// window). To avoid killing a real runner on its normal pullback, the stop is only active UNTIL
// the trend PROVES itself by travelling >= provenPts in its favor; after that only the pullback
// break exits. 0 = OFF.
adverseStopPts = input.float(40.0, "Adverse stop: cancel if it moves this far vs the dot (0=off, un-timed)", minval=0.0, step=5.0, group="Trend break")
provenPts      = input.float(80.0, "Adverse stop turns OFF once trend travels this far in its favor", minval=1.0, step=5.0, group="Trend break")
// After a cancel, a same-direction window usually STILL qualifies (the lookback still points
// that way), so without a cooldown the trend just re-latches a few bars later into the same
// failing move. Block a new SAME-direction latch for this many bars after a cancel. 0 = off.
cancelCool    = input.int(10, "Cooldown bars blocking same-dir re-latch after a cancel", minval=0, maxval=200, group="Trend break")

// EOD: END the live trend at session close so it mirrors the strategy's EOD flatten. A trend
// that spans the close does NOT carry over -- it ends (end dot), and next session a continuing
// move re-detects as a FRESH trend with a new start dot. No lock, so re-detection is immediate.
// Robust to empty windows / early-close / holidays via a session TIME GAP (like the strategy).
enableEod  = input.bool(true,  "EOD: end trend at session close (mirror strategy)", group="EOD (day trading)")
eodHour    = input.int(21, "EOD end hour (chart/London time)", minval=0, maxval=23, group="EOD (day trading)")
eodMin     = input.int(0,  "EOD end minute",                   minval=0, maxval=59, group="EOD (day trading)")
reopenHour = input.int(23, "Re-open hour (resume detection)",  minval=0, maxval=23, group="EOD (day trading)")
reopenMin  = input.int(0,  "Re-open minute",                   minval=0, maxval=59, group="EOD (day trading)")
eodTz      = input.string("Europe/London", "EOD timezone", options=["Europe/London","America/New_York","America/Chicago","UTC"], group="EOD (day trading)")

markStart  = input.bool(true, "Plot trend START dot",  group="Display")
markEnd    = input.bool(true, "Plot trend BREAK dot (incl. confirm-window cancels)",  group="Display")

//=============================
// OLS helper over the last N bars (manual, so N can be dynamic).
// Returns slope, r2, and the fit-line value at the OLDEST bar (x=0 intercept b0)
// via tuple. run = |slope|*(N-1).
//=============================
// NUMERICALLY STABLE OLS. The naive Σy² − (Σy)²/N formula catastrophically cancels when
// prices are large (~29500) and N is big: both terms are ~1.6e11 and their tiny difference
// (~1e6) is lost to float precision -> garbage variance/slope/R^2 (the "slope ramps from 0"
// bug). Fix: CENTER y on the first sample (yRef) so accumulated values stay small. x is
// small already (0..N-1) so it needs no centering. Variances/covariance are shift-invariant,
// so centering changes nothing mathematically -- only the precision.
olsScan(int N) =>
    float yRef = srcPrice[N - 1]   // oldest bar in the window; subtract to keep sums small
    float sx  = 0.0
    float sy  = 0.0
    float sxx = 0.0
    float syy = 0.0
    float sxy = 0.0
    for i = 0 to N - 1
        x = float(N - 1 - i)          // current bar -> x=N-1, oldest -> x=0
        y = srcPrice[i] - yRef        // centered price (small magnitude)
        sx  += x
        sy  += y
        sxx += x * x
        syy += y * y
        sxy += x * y
    fN    = float(N)
    varX  = sxx - sx * sx / fN
    varY  = syy - sy * sy / fN
    covXY = sxy - sx * sy / fN
    float slope = na
    float r2    = na
    float b0    = na
    if varX > 0 and varY > 0
        slope := covXY / varX
        r2    := (covXY * covXY) / (varX * varY)
        // b0 is the fit value at x=0 (oldest bar); add yRef back to undo the centering
        b0    := yRef + (sy / fN) - slope * (sx / fN)
    [slope, r2, b0]

//=============================
// State
//=============================
var int    state      = 0      // 0 = FLAT (scanning), 1 = LIVE
var int    anchorBar  = na     // bar_index of the trend's oldest (start) bar
var float  startPrice = na     // actual price at the anchor bar (for travel measure)
var float  liveSlope  = na     // locked slope (pts per bar), signed
var int    liveDir    = 0      // +1 up, -1 down
var float  liveExtreme = na    // running high (up) / low (down) reached while live

// same-direction re-entry lock: after a break, remember the direction, the extreme the
// trend reached, and how far it travelled. Block a NEW trend in the SAME direction until
// price retraces reEntryFrac of that travel back off the extreme (a genuine reversal).
var int    lockDir     = 0
var float  lockExtreme = na
var float  lockTravel  = na

// ---- dot-event tracking (for clean CSV export of each trend's lifespan) ----
var int    dotBar      = na    // bar_index where the START dot fired
var int    dotTime     = na    // time (ms) of the START dot bar
var float  dotPrice    = na    // close at the START dot bar
var int    winNbars    = na    // winning window N of the current live trend (bars looked back)

// ---- confirmation-cancel cooldown: block a same-direction re-latch right after a cancel ----
var int    cancelDir   = 0     // direction that was just cancelled (+1/-1), 0 = none
var int    cancelBar   = na    // bar_index of the cancel (cooldown measured from here)

bool  firedStart = false
bool  firedBreak = false
int   brokeDirEnded = 0     // direction of the trend that ended THIS bar (+1 up / -1 down / 0 none)

// ---- diagnostics exposed to the data window (per-bar, reset each bar) ----
float dbgExtreme  = na      // running extreme while live
float dbgPullback = na      // how far price has retraced off the extreme (pts)
float dbgLiveR2   = na      // R^2 of the live refit this bar (drawing only, not the break)
float dbgLiveSlope = na     // slope of the live refit this bar

//=============================
// Clear the same-direction re-entry lock once price has genuinely reversed:
// retraced reEntryFrac of the completed move back off its extreme.
//=============================
if lockDir != 0 and not na(lockExtreme)
    _need = reEntryFrac * lockTravel
    if lockDir < 0 and high >= lockExtreme + _need
        lockDir := 0
    else if lockDir > 0 and low <= lockExtreme - _need
        lockDir := 0

// expire the post-cancel cooldown once cancelCool bars have passed
if cancelDir != 0 and (na(cancelBar) or bar_index - cancelBar >= cancelCool)
    cancelDir := 0

//=============================
// EOD (mirror strategy): end a live trend at session close, block new detection in the
// [flatten,reopen) window, and treat a real session TIME GAP (weekend/holiday/early close) as a
// close too -- so a trend never carries over a closed session and next session re-detects fresh.
//=============================
_nowMin  = hour(time, eodTz) * 60 + minute(time, eodTz)
_flatMin = eodHour * 60 + eodMin
_openMin = reopenHour * 60 + reopenMin
_inWin   = _flatMin <= _openMin ? (_nowMin >= _flatMin and _nowMin < _openMin) : (_nowMin >= _flatMin or _nowMin < _openMin)
eodClosed = enableEod and _inWin
_windowEdge = eodClosed and not eodClosed[1]
_gapEdge    = enableEod and (time - time[1]) / 60000.0 > 60   // >60min gap = session break
eodEndEdge  = _windowEdge or _gapEdge

// end the live trend at the EOD edge (like a break, no lock) so it re-detects fresh next session
if eodEndEdge and state == 1
    firedBreak    := true
    brokeDirEnded := liveDir
    lockExtreme := liveExtreme
    lockTravel  := math.max(math.abs(liveExtreme - startPrice), 1.0)
    state       := 0
    anchorBar   := na
    liveSlope   := na
    liveDir     := 0
    liveExtreme := na

//=============================
// FLAT: scan windows to detect a new trend
//=============================
if state == 0
    float dSlope = na
    float dR2    = na
    float dB0    = na
    int   dN     = na
    _wmax = math.min(winMax, 4990)
    for N = winMin to _wmax by winStep
        if N >= 3 and bar_index >= N - 1
            [s, r2, b0] = olsScan(N)
            if not na(s)
                run = math.abs(s) * float(N - 1)
                if run >= runMinPts and r2 >= minR2
                    dir = s > 0 ? 1 : -1
                    // block re-detecting a trend in the still-locked direction, or a same-
                    // direction re-latch during the post-cancel cooldown
                    if dir != lockDir and dir != cancelDir and (na(dN) or (pickBest and r2 > dR2))
                        dSlope := s
                        dR2    := r2
                        dB0    := b0
                        dN     := N
    if not na(dN) and not eodClosed
        // latch the trend (blocked during the EOD closed window, mirroring the strategy)
        state      := 1
        anchorBar  := bar_index - (dN - 1)
        startPrice := close[dN - 1]                 // actual price at the anchor bar
        liveSlope  := dSlope
        liveDir    := dSlope > 0 ? 1 : -1
        liveExtreme := liveDir > 0 ? high : low
        firedStart := true
        dotBar     := bar_index          // the START dot is plotted HERE (not at anchorBar)
        dotTime    := time
        dotPrice   := close
        winNbars   := dN                 // winning window N (how many bars back the fit spanned)

//=============================
// LIVE: track the trend each bar. We still refit OLS over anchor->now to keep the live
// slope/R^2 diagnostics current, but we no longer DRAW a line -- the start/break dots plus
// the data-window columns carry the concept; a single OLS line across a long, bent, dynamic-
// pullback trend cut across price and looked wrong. The trend ends solely on a big pullback
// off the extreme (see break condition below).
//=============================
if state == 1
    _liveN = math.min(bar_index - anchorBar + 1, liveCap)
    // update the running extreme in the trend's direction
    liveExtreme := liveDir > 0 ? math.max(liveExtreme, high) : math.min(liveExtreme, low)

    // refit OLS over the live window (diagnostics only; no line drawn)
    [rs, rr2, rb0] = olsScan(_liveN)
    if not na(rs)
        liveSlope := rs

    // break condition: ONE rule only -- a big pullback off the extreme (a real reversal).
    // The live refit is diagnostics only; it does NOT decide the break,
    // so the trend can't end at the low on a fit metric. A down-trend ends when price
    // bounces effPullback above its low; an up-trend when price drops effPullback below
    // its high. This is knowable in real time and never lands the break at the turning point.
    // effPullback grows with how far the trend has already run (travel), so a far-travelled
    // runner needs a proportionally bigger reversal to end -- see pullbackFrac.
    _travel     = math.abs(liveExtreme - startPrice)
    effPullback = math.max(pullbackPts, _travel * pullbackFrac)
    brokeUp  = liveDir > 0 and close < liveExtreme - effPullback
    brokeDn  = liveDir < 0 and close > liveExtreme + effPullback

    // ---- confirmation window: cancel a false latch that reverses right after the dot ----
    // Only AFTER the latch bar (>=1 bar old) and within confirmMins bars of the START dot;
    // adverse move measured from the dot close. Requiring >=1 bar old prevents a trend from
    // latching and cancelling on its OWN birth bar (a life=0 zero-length "trend" that drew a
    // stray second END marker one bar after a real break). A cancel drops the trend without a
    // lock so the direction can re-fire after the cooldown.
    _age       = bar_index - dotBar
    _inConfirm = confirmMins > 0 and _age >= 1 and _age <= confirmMins
    _adverse   = liveDir > 0 ? (dotPrice - low) : (high - dotPrice)   // + = moved against the trend
    _confirmCancel = _inConfirm and _adverse >= confirmAdvPts
    // un-timed adverse stop: active at ANY age until the trend has PROVEN itself (favorable
    // travel from the dot >= provenPts). _favTravel is measured from the dot close in-direction.
    _favTravel = liveDir > 0 ? (liveExtreme - dotPrice) : (dotPrice - liveExtreme)
    _proven    = _favTravel >= provenPts
    _adverseStop = adverseStopPts > 0 and _age >= 1 and not _proven and _adverse >= adverseStopPts
    cancelLatch = _confirmCancel or _adverseStop

    // ---- publish diagnostics for THIS live bar ----
    dbgExtreme   := liveExtreme
    dbgPullback  := liveDir > 0 ? (liveExtreme - close) : (close - liveExtreme)  // + = retraced off extreme
    dbgLiveR2    := rr2
    dbgLiveSlope := rs

    if cancelLatch
        // false start: end this (short-lived) trend. It does NOT arm the re-entry lock
        // (lockDir stays 0), but the cooldown below blocks a same-direction re-latch into
        // the same failing move. Draw the normal END marker -- a cancel is just a very short
        // trend that ended. Set lockExtreme/lockTravel so the EVT_ export reports this
        // trend's real extreme/travel on the break row (these do not arm a lock).
        firedBreak    := true
        brokeDirEnded := liveDir
        lockExtreme := liveExtreme
        lockTravel  := math.max(math.abs(liveExtreme - startPrice), 1.0)
        cancelDir   := liveDir
        cancelBar   := bar_index
        state       := 0
        anchorBar   := na
        liveSlope   := na
        liveDir     := 0
        liveExtreme := na
    else if brokeUp or brokeDn
        firedBreak := true
        // arm the same-direction re-entry lock, keyed to this move's total travel
        lockDir     := liveDir
        lockExtreme := liveExtreme
        lockTravel  := math.max(math.abs(liveExtreme - startPrice), 1.0)
        // NO lookahead: the trend is only KNOWN to be over on THIS (confirmation) bar --
        // the bar price has bounced pullbackPts off the extreme. A strategy could act here,
        // not at the extreme (which you can't identify until the bounce completes). The end
        // marker is drawn (as a plotshape) at the confirmation bar in the Visuals section.
        brokeDirEnded := liveDir       // remember which trend just ended (for marker placement)
        state       := 0
        anchorBar   := na
        liveSlope   := na
        liveDir     := 0
        liveExtreme := na

//=============================
// Visuals
//=============================
plotshape(markStart and firedStart and liveDir > 0, "up trend start",   shape.circle, location.belowbar, color=color.new(color.lime, 0), size=size.small)
plotshape(markStart and firedStart and liveDir < 0, "down trend start", shape.circle, location.abovebar, color=color.new(color.red,  0), size=size.small)
// trend BREAK (confirmation bar): bright X, placed on the side the ended trend was heading.
// A down-trend ends with an up-bounce -> mark ABOVE; an up-trend ends -> mark BELOW.
plotshape(markEnd and firedBreak and brokeDirEnded < 0, "down trend break", shape.xcross, location.abovebar, color=color.new(color.yellow, 0), size=size.small, text="END")
plotshape(markEnd and firedBreak and brokeDirEnded > 0, "up trend break",   shape.xcross, location.belowbar, color=color.new(color.yellow, 0), size=size.small, text="END")
// (trend BREAK marker is drawn as a label at the break price inside the LIVE block above)

//=============================
// Version label — bottom-right (same style as slope_strategy)
//=============================
var table cityTable = table.new(position.bottom_right, 1, 1,
     bgcolor      = color.new(color.black, 20),
     border_width = 1,
     border_color = color.new(color.gray, 50))
if barstate.islast
    table.cell(cityTable, 0, 0, "Galway", text_color=color.yellow, text_size=size.small, bgcolor=color.new(color.navy, 10))

//=============================
// PARAM columns -- the actual input values, plotted every bar so any export SELF-DOCUMENTS
// exactly which settings produced it (no more guessing what was on the chart). Constant per
// export; read them off any row.
//=============================
plot(winMin,        "P_winMin",       color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(winMax,        "P_winMax",       color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(runMinPts,     "P_runMinPts",    color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(minR2,         "P_minR2",        color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(pullbackPts,   "P_pullbackPts",  color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(pullbackFrac,  "P_pullbackFrac", color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(reEntryFrac,   "P_reEntryFrac",  color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(confirmMins,   "P_confirmMins",  color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(confirmAdvPts, "P_confirmAdvPts",color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(adverseStopPts,"P_adverseStopPts",color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(provenPts,     "P_provenPts",    color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(cancelCool,    "P_cancelCool",   color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(enableEod ? 1 : 0, "P_enableEod",color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(eodHour,       "P_eodHour",      color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(reopenHour,    "P_reopenHour",   color=na, display=display.data_window)

//=============================
// Diagnostics (data window)
//=============================
plot(state == 1 ? 1 : 0, "live (1/0)",        color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(liveSlope,          "locked slope pts/bar", color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(state == 1 ? float(bar_index - anchorBar + 1) : na, "live length (bars)", color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(state == 1 ? float(winNbars) : na, "winning N (bars back)", color=na, display=display.data_window)
// --- break-diagnostic columns (fresh export will show WHY/WHERE a break fires) ---
plot(dbgExtreme,   "dbg extreme",        color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(dbgPullback,  "dbg pullback off ext", color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(dbgLiveR2,    "dbg live R2",        color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(dbgLiveSlope, "dbg live slope",     color=na, display=display.data_window)

// --- EVENT-EXPORT columns: non-na ONLY on the bar the dot fires -----------------
// START rows: EVT_start_dir (+1 up / -1 down) and EVT_start_px (dot price).
// BREAK rows: EVT_break_dir (dir of the trend that ended), plus its lifespan:
//   EVT_life_bars (dot->break bars), EVT_life_min (minutes), EVT_travel (pts
//   start->extreme), EVT_extreme (the high/low reached), EVT_start_px_of_ended.
// Filter the exported CSV to rows where EVT_start_dir OR EVT_break_dir is non-blank.
plot(firedStart ? liveDir : na,                        "EVT_start_dir", color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(firedStart ? dotPrice : na,                       "EVT_start_px",  color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(firedStart ? float(winNbars) : na,                "EVT_win_N",     color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(firedBreak ? brokeDirEnded : na,                  "EVT_break_dir", color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(firedBreak ? float(bar_index - dotBar) : na,      "EVT_life_bars", color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(firedBreak ? (time - dotTime) / 60000.0 : na,     "EVT_life_min",  color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(firedBreak ? math.abs(lockExtreme - dotPrice) : na,"EVT_travel",   color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(firedBreak ? lockExtreme : na,                    "EVT_extreme",   color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(firedBreak ? dotPrice : na,                       "EVT_start_px_of_ended", color=na, display=display.data_window)
